course: dictionary
lesson: 14951
title: Relapse: falling back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A relapse is when something bad comes back after you thought it had gone. «Mum said the flu was gone, but she had a relapse.» She seemed better, then became ill again. That is a relapse.
explain: You can also relapse into a habit. «Sam stopped biting his nails, but after a stressful week he relapsed.» Sam went back to a habit he had given up. As a verb, relapse means to fall back into illness or a bad state: «The patient began to relapse.»
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If someone who got better becomes ill again, relapse fits. The clues «seemed better» and «stopped» tell you the word means going back to something bad.
fact: Relapse means becoming ill again after seeming to get better.
fact: Relapse can also mean going back to a bad habit after stopping it.
fact: As a verb, relapse means to fall back into illness or a bad state.
fact: «Relapse» is a noun (a relapse, relapses), and «relapse» is also a verb (relapsed, relapsing).
fact: «Relapse into» means to fall back into an old way, such as «relapse into naughty ways».
exercise: «Mum's cold had gone, but after two days it came back. She had a relapse.» What does relapse mean here? | *Becoming ill again after seeming to get better | Feeling very happy and well | Going on a long trip | Forgetting a word
exercise: Lucy stopped eating sweets, but after a bad day she went back to them. What is the best word for this? | *Relapse | Relax | Repeat | Explore
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to fall back into a bad state: «The patient began to relapse after the new medicine stopped working.» | working | patient | medicine | *relapse
test: «After weeks of feeling fine, Grandad began to relapse.» What does relapse mean here? | Run quickly up the hill | Get a new job | Feel very proud of himself | *Fall back into being ill
test: Which sentence uses relapse in the right way? | *After stopping smoking, he relapsed and had a cigarette. | She relapsed her new bike to the shop. | The bell relapsed at noon. | The sun relapsed behind the hill.
exam: Which word best matches relapse in the sentence «He stopped the bad habit, but then fell back into it»? | reward | rescue | *relapse | regret
